{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S3 (a8ea): Config-driven type mapping + type-granular skip\n\n## Context / Problem\nEpic 3d7a adds a config-driven mapping seam (S1: `mapping_config.MappingLayer` with a\n`type_map` axis, `SKIP=\"skip\"`, `resolve_for_project`, `validate`). S2 made STATUS\nconfig-driven — the template: `config.effective_status_map` (`config.py:77`) threads a\nper-project `status_map` through the Backend port into the field mappers; `rebar-status:`\nstamp in `outbound_labels.py`; reverse-map-free inbound `recover_status_label` (`:152`). TYPE\nis still hard-coded: `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` (`adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py:40` =\n`{bug,story,task,epic}`), `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` (`config.py:13`), with three create sites\ndefaulting an unknown type to Jira `Task`/capitalized passthrough. Distinct types can collapse\nto one Jira type (lossy). Syncable = `get_args(TicketType)` (`types.py:23`) −\n`EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` = `{bug,epic,story,task}` = keys of `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`. (S3 type-only.)\n\n## Approach\nThree outcomes for `ticket_type`: **remap** (effective type map), **skip** (per-project\ntype-granular exclusion), **FAIL-CLOSED** on an undecided syncable type. Round-trip safety:\nNEW `rebar-type:` annotation label symmetric with `rebar-status:`, recovered reverse-map-free.\n\n### Finding 1 (G7) — fail-closed fires ONCE UP-FRONT, before the mutation loop\nParent AC (\"load-time fail-closed on undecided types\") is PRIMARY. `effective_status_map` is\ninvoked LAZILY per-ticket in the differ loop, so a per-ticket-resolved gate would NOT fire\nbefore mutations. FIX:\n- NEW `config.effective_type_map(project_key, root)` mirrors `effective_status_map` (`:77`):\n  `builtin=MappingLayer(type_map=LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA)` ← `resolve_for_project`, drop `SKIP`.\n- NEW `config.assert_type_decisions_complete(project_key, root)`: every syncable type\n  (`get_args(TicketType) − EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES`, minus the effective excluded set) must be\n  DECIDED — target OR `SKIP` — else raise `MappingConfigError`.\n- WIRING (proves fail-closed-before-mutation): call it ONCE at the top of\n  `compute_outbound_mutations` (`outbound_differ.py:298`) — after config load `:377`, BEFORE\n  `_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets` (`:381`) and the per-ticket loop (`:430`) — over the\n  DISTINCT project keys of `local_tickets` (via `projects_store.resolve_project` with\n  `config.projects_mapping`/`config.repo_root`, as `_effective_status_map_for` does at\n  `:454`/`:479`). Create-mapper raising is only a SECONDARY guard. (S1's `mapping_config.validate`\n  stays uncalled — S4's concern; S3 does not depend on it.)\n\n### Finding 3 (G6) — reverse TYPE map source for the lossy-stamp rule\n`_desired_type_annotation` stamps only when the forward target does NOT reverse to this\nlocal type — needs a Jira→local TYPE reverse map. `config.py` has none, and\n`outbound_labels.py` imports ONLY `config`. FIX: NEW `config.jira_to_local_type` mirroring\n`config.jira_to_local_status` (`:64`) — reverse of `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`, lock-stepped with\n`inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE` (`:105`) via a parity test.\n\n### Finding 4 (G6/G1G2) — thread type_map through ALL THREE OutboundMapper impls\nS2's `status_map` runs through THREE concrete `map_local_to_remote` bodies plus the shared\nfield mappers; `type_map` must follow every one or the differ's `type_map=` kwarg hits a\nsignature lacking it → `TypeError`. Add `type_map: dict[str,str] | None = None` (beside\n`status_map`) to: (1) `OutboundMapper.map_local_to_remote` Protocol (`_backend.py:372`);\n(2) Cloud `JiraBackend.map_local_to_remote` (`jira/backend.py:73`, forwards `status_map`\n`:89`) → forward into `_map_local_to_jira_fields`; (3) DC (`jira_datacenter/backend.py:121`)\n→ forward into `_map_local_to_dc_fields`; (4) `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields`\n(`:101`/`:108`) — resolve issuetype via `type_map` (replacing coerce `:143`), fail-closed;\n(5) DC `_map_local_to_dc_fields` (coerce `jira_datacenter/backend.py:86`) — same. NEW\n`outbound_differ._effective_type_map_for` mirrors `_effective_status_map_for` (`:272`);\n`_compute_outbound_create_mutation` (`outbound_mutation_builders.py:37`) passes `type_map=`.\n\n### Finding 2 (G1G2/G6) — acli.py:282 needs a MATERIALLY DIFFERENT rewrite\n`adapters/jira/acli.py:282` (`JiraClient.create_issue`, the transport's OWN method, NOT the\n`OutboundMapper` port) computes `issue_type = ticket_data.get(\"ticket_type\",\"Task\")\n.capitalize()` — passthrough capitalize, NO map, NO `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA` import; an unknown\nsyncable type (\"spike\") is capitalized through, never coerced to Task. FIX (distinct from the\nmapper paths): import `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`, resolve `issue_type` via the effective type map\n(carried on the create payload beside `_bridge_target_project`), fail-closed on undecided type.\n\n## Surface-parity census — stamp + inbound + prefix filters\n- Stamp: NEW `outbound_labels._REBAR_TYPE_LABEL_PREFIX=\"rebar-type:\"`,\n  `_desired_type_annotation` (mirror `_desired_status_annotation` `:89`, using\n  `config.jira_to_local_type`), `_diff_type_annotation_labels` (mirror `:114`). Threaded at\n  BOTH `outbound_mutation_builders.py` sites: create `:81`/`:138`; update `:276`/`:281`.\n- Inbound: NEW `inbound_fields.recover_type_label` (mirror `recover_status_label` `:152`) +\n  `_LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB` from `get_args(TicketType)`; at `:311-313`, label-over-raw `:326`.\n- Per-project excluded set replaces the single `EXCLUDED_SYNC_TYPES` read (`:377`) at BOTH\n  consumers: `:430` (loop) and `:519` (`_compute_outbound_select_absent_gets`).\n- `rebar-type:` added to ALL FOUR prefix tuples: `outbound_labels.py:34` `_EXCLUDED_PREFIXES`\n  (re-export `outbound_differ.py:77`); `inbound_collection_diffs.py:88` `_EXCLUDED_PREFIXES`\n  (re-export `inbound_differ.py:31`; read `reconcile_check.py:96`); `differ.py:105`\n  `_BRIDGE_INTERNAL_LABEL_PREFIXES`; `inbound_translate.py:58` `_BRIDGE_INTERNAL_TAG_PREFIXES`\n  (keeps omission of `\"imported:\"`).\n\n## Scope\n`config.py` (effective_type_map, assert_type_decisions_complete, effective_excluded_sync_types,\njira_to_local_type); `_backend.py:372`; all three OutboundMapper impls (Cloud\n`jira/backend.py:73`, DC `jira_datacenter/backend.py:121`) + field mappers\n(`_map_local_to_jira_fields`, DC `_map_local_to_dc_fields:86`); `acli.py:282`;\n`outbound_labels.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_differ.py` (up-front gate,\n`_effective_type_map_for`, per-project excluded set), `inbound_fields.py`,\n`inbound_collection_diffs.py`, `differ.py`, `inbound_translate.py`. Module-size cap 800 LOC\n(target 200-500) — additions small.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria (`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_type_mapping.py`)\n- [ ] `test_fail_closed_fires_before_mutation_loop` — undecided syncable type raises\n  `MappingConfigError` from `compute_outbound_mutations` before any mutation is built.\n- [ ] `test_skip_is_a_valid_type_decision` — `SKIP` passes the gate and excludes the ticket.\n- [ ] `test_effective_type_map_default_equals_builtin` — no `[mapping]` ⇒ `LOCAL_TYPE_TO_JIRA`;\n  a project `type_map` remaps.\n- [ ] `test_type_skip_excludes_ticket_both_consumers` — excluded at `:430` AND `:519`.\n- [ ] `test_type_map_threaded_through_all_three_mappers` — `type_map=` reaches Protocol,\n  Cloud (`jira/backend.py:73`) + DC (`jira_datacenter/backend.py:121`), no `TypeError`.\n- [ ] `test_acli_create_issue_maps_and_fails_closed` — acli maps via type map, raises on\n  undecided type (no capitalize passthrough).\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_label_stamped_when_lossy` — collapsing types stamp `rebar-type:` at\n  create + update sites via `config.jira_to_local_type`.\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_label_recovered_reverse_map_free` — `recover_type_label` restores it.\n- [ ] `test_rebar_type_prefix_excluded_all_four_tuples` — filtered by all four tuples.\n- [ ] `test_jira_to_local_type_parity` — == `inbound_fields._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE`.\n- [ ] `test_local_type_vocab_derived_from_ticket_type` — `_LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB` ==\n  `get_args(TicketType)`.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787356462211571001,"uuid":"9d34ae7b-8288-4646-90d6-25d472ef234f"}